1772498490759463	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuOA		item.create	bn-3nv	{"description":"When BOTTY_LOG is set to a file path, the server writes tracing logs there (append mode).\nThe file log uses botty=info minimum so server lifecycle events (signal handling, agent\nspawn/exit, shutdown) are always captured even without --verbose.\n\n## Progress\n- [x] Implementation in src/telemetry.rs — done, builds clean, uncommitted on main\n- [ ] Test manually (run server with BOTTY_LOG, verify log file gets entries)\n- [ ] Cut release\n\n## Notes\n- Concern: running `cargo test` may interfere with a running botty server (tests spawn\n  their own server instances on the same socket). Skip integration tests if server is live.\n- The implementation uses a single writer (file only, not tee'd to stderr) when BOTTY_LOG\n  is set. This is fine for daemon mode where stderr goes nowhere anyway.","kind":"task","title":"BOTTY_LOG env var for file logging"}	blake3:k5Cc8yne2DWnweQ30c6yFfqIRXuPAQSKT8F8O5kDfTg
