1772676840055620	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuQA		item.comment	bn-1ck	{"body":"## Migration feasibility assessment (v0.2.7)\n\nTested asupersync v0.2.7 from crates.io + local repo at ~/repos/asupersync. Found significant API gaps that block a straightforward tokio replacement.\n\n### What works (confirmed compiling)\n\n- `RuntimeBuilder::new().build()` + `block_on()` — runtime entry point\n- `RuntimeHandle::spawn()` — fire-and-forget tasks (not a free fn, need handle)\n- `UnixStream::connect()`, `UnixListener::bind()`, `.accept()` — same signatures as tokio\n- `UnixStream::into_split()` → `(OwnedReadHalf, OwnedWriteHalf)` — same as tokio\n- `sleep(wall_now(), duration)` — works but needs Time param\n- `timeout(wall_now(), duration, future)` — works but needs Time param\n- `signal::sigterm()`, `sigwinch()`, etc — returns Signal with `.recv().await`\n- `Select<A, B>::new(f1, f2).await` → `Either::Left`/`Right` — replaces 2-branch select!\n- `spawn_blocking(f).await` → returns T directly\n- `BufReader::new()` — async buffered reader exists\n- `AsyncReadExt::read()`, `AsyncWriteExt::write_all()`, `.shutdown()` — available\n- `io::Lines` stream — stream-based line iteration (replaces read_line loops)\n\n### Blocking gaps\n\n1. **No async stdin/stdout** — `tokio::io::stdin()`/`stdout()` have no equivalent. Used in attach.rs for terminal I/O bridge. Would need a shim (spawn_blocking + channel).\n\n2. **No `read_line()` on BufReader** — `AsyncBufRead` only has `fill_buf()`/`consume()`. No `AsyncBufReadExt` trait. The `Lines` stream exists but is iterator-based, not a direct method. All protocol parsing uses `read_line()` extensively.\n\n3. **`Mutex::lock(cx)` requires Cx** — capability context must be threaded through every lock site. Can't do `mutex.lock().await` without Cx.\n\n4. **`broadcast::send(cx)` and `recv(cx)` require Cx** — same issue. Server event broadcast uses these heavily.\n\n5. **`race!` macro is a placeholder** — the macro_rules version just drops futures. Real implementation is via `cx.race()` or proc-macro, both requiring Cx. Low-level `Select<A,B>` works without Cx for 2-branch cases.\n\n6. **`interval()` is sync, not async** — `tick(now)` is synchronous polling, not `.tick().await`. Server heartbeat loop needs restructuring.\n\n7. **`sleep()`/`timeout()` need Time param** — every call needs `wall_now()` prepended. Manageable but pervasive (dozens of call sites).\n\n8. **`spawn` is on RuntimeHandle, not a free function** — need to pass handle around or store globally. tokio::spawn() just works anywhere.\n\n### Cx threading is the fundamental blocker\n\nThe Cx requirement on Mutex, broadcast, and race means this isn't a surface-level API rename — it's an architectural change. Every async function touching a Mutex or broadcast channel needs Cx threaded through its signature. This affects server/mod.rs (20 refs), testing.rs (14 refs), and cascades through callers.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nBlocked pending upstream resolution of gaps. Filed/will file GitHub issue requesting:\n- Async stdin/stdout\n- read_line() / AsyncBufReadExt\n- Cx-free convenience APIs for Mutex and broadcast (or ambient Cx)\n- Working race! macro without Cx requirement\n- Async interval tick"}	blake3:nE52D7XSfgXwOeplcFRmtfgaUR5BcbvxNvNoznh4yOg
1772677350939632	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuQQ		item.comment	bn-1ck	{"body":"Filed upstream issue for API gaps: https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/asupersync/issues/17 — blocked pending response."}	blake3:SLgVGNeVNhxXvo15WktzriSaZPu5-Su3nY2zrMex0L8
1772718568755927	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEz6wE		item.comment	bn-1ck	{"body":"got a response from Dicklesworthstone. please read it using the gh tool"}	blake3:5sXl74uGDezn6VN5XXl_h1TIZrHO6S5TI0V0SUP_DJM
1772719119057208	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuQg		item.comment	bn-1ck	{"body":"## Upstream response (2026-03-05)\n\nDicklesworthstone responded on GH issue #17. Key corrections:\n\n- **stdin/stdout exists**: ChildStdin/ChildStdout with AsyncWrite/AsyncRead in src/process.rs (not general-purpose like tokio::io::stdin(), but usable)\n- **race! macro works**: fully implemented proc-macro in asupersync-macros/src/race.rs, requires Cx\n- **read_line() added**: commit 449c317 adds AsyncBufRead::read_line()\n\nCx threading on Mutex/broadcast/race is intentional (cancel-correctness), not a gap. Virtual time on interval is by design for deterministic testing.\n\n### Revised migration assessment\n\nBlockers reduced to:\n1. **Cx threading** — architectural rework to pass Cx through server handlers, attach bridge, etc. This is the main cost.\n2. **stdin/stdout** — ChildStdin/ChildStdout exist but may not cover our use case (we need raw terminal stdin, not child process pipes). Needs investigation.\n3. **interval** — sync tick(now) means restructuring poll loops. Manageable.\n\nStill proceeding with migration."}	blake3:BABrSS_BbHo_TwwvjM9G9uL6vHT7PmAgE4e9loyMgA4
